==Strategy==
These five stages are substantially harder, mostly due to the presence of [[Le'Behemoth]], who fully covers True Assassin's blindspot and has very high stats, reaching 27200 damage and 760000 health at 200%, not to mention his 1600000 Shield that blocks all status effects, towering even the nasty 300% Dark Otters. The peons can also block many Single Attacks from DPS units while True Assassin cripples them with status effects. While raw damage is enough to kill the lesser threats, means of removing either True Assassin or Le'Behemoth are vital to quickly clear the stage or there won't be any ground to sustain the fight. At the very least some reliable Shield Piercing unit should be used to address Le'Behemoth to greatly reduce his effective health and render him vulnerable to status effects.

===Recommended Units===
*Awakened Bahamut - While Bahamut won't be of much use against Le'Behemoth, he can still quickly take out the Dark Otters, especially when supported and talented with Explosions. He also helps with cleanup later if Le'Behemoth is out of the way.
*Supercar - With 100% chance to Knockback Traited Enemies and Pierce Shields at low range, Supercar can possibly slip by True Assassin's LD attacks and reach Le'Behemoth, as Le'Behemoth has a long attack cycle of just over 6 seconds.
*Jelly Dumpling - Jelly Dumpling is one of the better means to reach True Assassin in the back through its powerful level 7 Wave Attacks that whittle it over time. The Wave can also clear Squire Rels, damage/destroy Aku Doge's Shield and force Doge Dark to flinch, giving Shield Piercers a better shot at Le'Behemoth.
